# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Bun loads `.env` automatically for
# anything run from the repo root, so neither the Pod spec nor code has to change.
#
# Only variables you have to supply yourself belong here. The devcontainer's
# Pod spec (generated by scripts/dev-pod.sh) already provides DATABASE_URL, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS,
# ALLOW_INSECURE_DEV_AUTH and the SMTP_* pair.

# Signing key for the local login route. Generate one with:
#
#     openssl rand -base64 32
#
# HS256 requires a key at least as long as its hash output, so the server
# refuses anything under 32 encoded bytes.
#
# Leave this unset and the devcontainer still starts, because its Pod spec sets
# ALLOW_INSECURE_DEV_AUTH=1. The server then trusts X-Actor-Id / X-Actor-Roles
# headers verbatim and registers no `POST /auth/login` at all (server.ts). The
# web UI cannot get a token in that state, so every sign-in fails with a 404
# that reads like a routing bug. The startup log says `AUTH DISABLED: ...`
# whenever this applies: check it first when login misbehaves.
#
# `bash scripts/dev-up.sh` needs no entry here: it generates this key once in
# `container/.auth-secret` and passes it to the server it starts. Set it here
# only when you start the server by hand. Demo accounts come from
# `bun run seed`.
AUTH_JWT_SECRET=
